T150	Quotation 33059 33082	"But you are a mirage,"
T151	Cue 33083 33087	said
T152	Entity 33088 33094	Kovrin
T153	Entity 32943 32951	the monk
T154	Quotation 33096 33171	"Why are you here and sitting still? That does not fit in with the legend."
T155	Quotation 33172 33195	"That does not matter,"
T156	Entity 33196 33204	the monk
T157	Cue 33205 33213	answered
T158	Quotation 33276 33373	"The legend, the mirage, and I are all the products of your excited imagination. I am a phantom."
T159	Quotation 33374 33397	"Then you don't exist?"
T160	Cue 33398 33402	said
T161	Entity 33403 33409	Kovrin
T162	Quotation 33411 33439	"You can think as you like,"
T163	Cue 33440 33444	said
T164	Entity 33445 33453	the monk
T165	Quotation 33475 33567	"I exist in your imagination, and your imagination is part of nature, so I exist in nature."
T166	Cue 33687 33691	said
T167	Entity 33692 33698	Kovrin
T168	Quotation 33568 33686	"You have a very old, wise, and extremely expressive face, as though you really had lived more than a thousand years,"
T169	Quotation 33700 33840	"I did not know that my imagination was capable of creating such phenomena. But why do you look at me with such enthusiasm? Do you like me?"
T170	Quotation 33841 34176	"Yes, you are one of those few who are justly called the chosen of God. You do the service of eternal truth. Your thoughts, your designs, the marvellous studies you are engaged in, and all your life, bear the Divine, the heavenly stamp, seeing that they are consecrated to the rational and the beautiful-- that is, to what is eternal."
T171	Quotation 34177 34296	"You said 'eternal truth.' . . . But is eternal truth of use to man and within his reach, if there is no eternal life?"
T172	Quotation 34297 34321	"There is eternal life,"
T173	Cue 34322 34326	said
T174	Entity 34327 34335	the monk
T175	Quotation 34337 34380	"Do you believe in the immortality of man?"
T176	Quotation 34381 34948	"Yes, of course. A grand, brilliant future is in store for you men. And the more there are like you on earth, the sooner will this future be realised. Without you who serve the higher principle and live in full understanding and freedom, mankind would be of little account; developing in a natural way, it would have to wait a long time for the end of its earthly history. You will lead it some thousands of years earlier into the kingdom of eternal truth-- and therein lies your supreme service. You are the incarnation of the blessing of God, which rests upon men."
T177	Quotation 34949 34990	"And what is the object of eternal life?"
T178	Cue 34991 34996	asked
T179	Entity 34997 35003	Kovrin
T180	Quotation 35005 35230	"As of all life-- enjoyment. True enjoyment lies in knowledge, and eternal life provides innumerable and inexhaustible sources of knowledge, and in that sense it has been said: 'In My Father's house there are many mansions.'"
T181	Quotation 35231 35281	"If only you knew how pleasant it is to hear you!"
T182	Cue 35282 35286	said
T183	Entity 35287 35293	Kovrin
T184	Quotation 35332 35349	"I am very glad."
T185	Quotation 35350 35512	"But I know that when you go away I shall be worried by the question of your reality. You are a phantom, an hallucination. So I am mentally deranged, not normal?"
T186	Quotation 35513 35849	"What if you are? Why trouble yourself? You are ill because you have overworked and exhausted yourself, and that means that you have sacrificed your health to the idea, and the time is near at hand when you will give up life itself to it. What could be better? That is the goal towards which all divinely endowed, noble natures strive."
T187	Quotation 35850 35905	"If I know I am mentally affected, can I trust myself?"
T188	Quotation 35906 36309	"And are you sure that the men of genius, whom all men trust, did not see phantoms, too? The learned say now that genius is allied to madness. My friend, healthy and normal people are only the common herd. Reflections upon the neurasthenia of the age, nervous exhaustion and degeneracy, et cetera, can only seriously agitate those who place the object of life in the present-- that is, the common herd."
T189	Quotation 36310 36362	"The Romans used to say: Mens sana in corpore sano."
T190	Quotation 36363 36680	"Not everything the Greeks and the Romans said is true. Exaltation, enthusiasm, ecstasy-- all that distinguishes prophets, poets, martyrs for the idea, from the common folk-- is repellent to the animal side of man-- that is, his physical health. I repeat, if you want to be healthy and normal, go to the common herd."
T191	Quotation 36681 36737	"Strange that you repeat what often comes into my mind,"
T192	Cue 36738 36742	said
T193	Entity 36743 36749	Kovrin
T194	Quotation 36751 36884	"It is as though you had seen and overheard my secret thoughts. But don't let us talk about me. What do you mean by 'eternal truth'?"
T195	Quotation 37138 37166	"The hallucination is over,"
T196	Cue 37167 37171	said
T197	Entity 37013 37017	monk
T198	Entity 37172 37178	Kovrin
T199	Quotation 37196 37210	"It's a pity."
